From 81e9cb5c7ef16660919a1c33b96117682812c3fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fix <fix@localhost>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 03:31:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Never abort() on recoverable failures (fix companion + fork
 crashes)

Zygisk runs this code inside the zygote fork child (pre*Specialize),
the freshly specialized target process incl. system_server
(post*Specialize) and the module companion daemon (zygiskd64).
abort() in any of these contexts kills the forked app, system_server
(soft reboot) or the whole companion daemon, and a dead companion then
makes the NEXT fork abort on connectCompanion() failure - a cascade
observed in the field (tombstones with zygisk_companion_entry+708 and
SIGABRT inside nativeForkAndSpecialize).

- companion (handleFileRequest): a broken client connection, failed
  open()/mmap() during INITIALIZE or any other request failure now
  logs LOGW/LOGE and drops that request instead of aborting; state is
  committed only after every step succeeded
- zygote side (initialize/isInitialized/shouldEnableForPackage/
  fetchResources/isUseBinderInterceptors): any socket I/O or fd failure
  degrades to "module not injected into this process"
- dex.c: never abort post-specialize; clear pending JNI exceptions on
  every failure path; degrade when binder interceptors are unavailable
- binder.c: fix reply parcel native pointer (was reading the data
  parcel twice); clear pending exceptions on lookup failures
- process.c: survive GetStringUTFChars failures instead of
  strdup(NULL) crashes
- main.c: resource_map_fd/resource_map_file return NULL on failure
- main_riru.cpp: refuse to load instead of crashing the Riru daemon
  when resources/module.prop are unusable; sprintf -> snprintf
- logger.h: LOGW/LOGE are always logged in release builds, LOGF now
  logs before aborting so future tombstones carry an abort message
- Loader.java: fix inverted isBinderInterceptorAvailable guards in
  unregisterRedirectBinder/callExecTransact
